[0m$ [0mcd "/home/nico/Documents/U/Co/U/4s/courses/interfaces/tareas/proyecto final/juego" && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG' && git log --oneline | head -3
Camera works in world space with a transformed level AABB

Following and clamping the camera in the level's local frame broke the moment
the L2 group rotated: local no longer maps to screen axes, so the local clamp
pinned the view to a spot the player was no longer at and they left the frame.
Now the level's four corners are transformed and their bounds drive the clamp,
which stays correct at any rotation angle.

Menu: _renderMenu was gated on a menuList element that does not exist in the
markup, so the difficulty and language rows never built. Removed the dead
vestigial reference, and the unwired duplicate rows in the pause screen.

Boot overlay is removed from the DOM after its fade instead of sitting there
painting its title across the menu.

Bosses get a brightness lift; they are the largest dark shapes on screen and
read as holes in the level without it.
